course: dictionary
lesson: 2984
title: Due: expected, owed, or exact
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word due has more than one meaning, so look at the words around it. In «return it by the due date», the clue is return: the book has to come back by a certain day, so due date means the day it is expected back.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The bus is due at four» means the bus is expected at four, and that makes sense in the sentence.
explain: «Due north» is a direction and means exactly north, not roughly north. «Due to» is a pair of words that means because of.
fact: Due has several meanings, so read the sentence to find the one that fits.
fact: «Due» can mean expected at a certain time, as in «the train is due at 4».
fact: «Due» can mean owed and must be paid, as in «the bill is due».
fact: «Due to» means because of, as in «the game was cancelled due to rain».
fact: «Due north» means exactly north.
exercise: «You scan or sign a library book out and return it by the due date, because others are waiting for it.» What does due date mean? | *The day something must be returned or finished | A date with a long history | The day you borrowed it | The day the library opens
exercise: «The game was cancelled due to rain.» What does due to mean here? | Expected at | Exactly north of | *Because of | Owed to
exercise: «NASA's Dragonfly is a nuclear-powered drone helicopter due to launch in 2028.» What does due to launch mean? | Owed money for a launch | Stuck on the ground | *Expected to launch at that time | Exactly north of the launch site
test: Ayesha's gas bill is due on Friday, so she must pay it by then. What does due mean in this sentence? | Expected to be finished | *Must be paid by a certain time | Lost | Very old
test: «The bus is due at four, but a traffic jam means it is late.» What does due at four mean? | Owed four pounds | *Expected to arrive at four | Four times as big | Exactly four miles away
exam: Mia says due means owed, but the sentence says «The homework is due on Monday.» Which meaning fits best? | Exactly north on Monday | Lost on Monday | Owed money on Monday | *Expected to be handed in on Monday
